github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6206#issuecomment-5534363989","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSd_FHw","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\" height=\"20px\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Uppercase templates bypass autoescape <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛨ Security</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>Removing <b><i>filename.lower()</i></b> makes <b><i>select_jinja_autoescape</i></b> return false for uppercase or mixed-case\n>extensions such as <b><i>page.HTML</i></b> and <b><i>icon.SVG</i></b>. Because this function supplies Jinja&#x27;s default\n>autoescape policy, untrusted values rendered by those templates are emitted without HTML escaping,\n>creating an XSS regression.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/flask/sansio/app.py[544]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6206/files#diff-c57b8f34cffef9948b35aec94cb2364f75c1a2854064a13bf8216603cb1f607bR544-R544)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+        return filename.endswith((\".html\", \".htm\", \".xml\", \".xhtml\", \".svg\"))\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The changed method now performs a case-sensitive <b><i>endswith</i></b> check. Flask installs this method as\n>Jinja&#x27;s autoescape callback when no custom policy is supplied, and the documentation identifies\n>these extensions as the templates for which autoescaping is enabled.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[src/flask/sansio/app.py[533-544]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/87c4a4e4673016954c71cf3a90e885c0f3b1d7d7/src/flask/sansio/app.py/#L533-L544)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[470-495]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/87c4a4e4673016954c71cf3a90e885c0f3b1d7d7/src/flask/app.py/#L470-L495)</code>\n> <code>[docs/templating.rst[15-26]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/87c4a4e4673016954c71cf3a90e885c0f3b1d7d7/docs/templating.rst/#L15-L26)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>Restore case-insensitive matching in `select_jinja_autoescape` so uppercase and mixed-case HTML, XML, XHTML, and SVG template extensions continue to enable Jinja autoescaping.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>The prior implementation normalized the filename before checking its extension. The new case-sensitive check changes public behavior and can disable escaping for templates such as `page.HTML`.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/flask/sansio/app.py[542-544]\n>- tests/test_templating.py[1-1]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- qodo-context:start -->\n<details><summary><strong>Context sources</strong></summary>\n\n<div>Review mode: <code>⚖️ Balanced</code></div>\n<!-- qodo-context:end -->\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Tip of the day</strong></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>💡 Did you know, you can route each action level your way: inline, summary, both, or drop</pre>\n\n<a href=\"https